\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Throned upon the awful Tree,
\par King of grief, I watch with Thee;
\par Darkness veils Thine anguish face,
\par None its lines of woe can trace,
\par None can tell what pangs unknown
\par Hold Thee silent and alone;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Silent through those three dread hours,
\par Wrestling with the evil powers;
\par Left alone with human sin,
\par Gloom around Thee and within,
\par Till the appointed time is nigh,
\par Till the Lamb of God may die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Hark that cry that peals aloud
\par Upward through the whelming cloud!
\par Thou, the Father's only Son,
\par Thou, His own Anointed One,
\par Thou dost assk Him- can it be:
\par Why hast Thou forsaken Me?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, should fear and anguish roll
\par Darkly o'er my sinful soul,
\par Thou, who once was thus bereft
\par That Thine own might ne'er be left,
\par Teach me by that bitter cry
\par In the gloom to know Thee nigh.
\par                                            Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

